+
+Experimental API `0.1-aurora-lighting.1` extends `0.1-aurora-atmosphere.2`.
+It is not supported by stock Horizon. Existing API lines retain their stage ABI.
+
+The material input appends `lighting: vec4<f32>` after `fog`:
+
+- RGB is the model's original biome/constant tint, normalized to 0..1, without
+  baked cardinal shade or ambient occlusion. Untinted models receive white.
+- Alpha is interpolated model ambient occlusion, quantized to 1..255 / 255.
+  With AO disabled it is 1. Zero is reserved for unavailable data.
+- Fluid meshes, merged LOD geometry and legacy vertex constructors carry zero
+  alpha. A pack must retain its old material path for them. This field is not
+  an opacity or an emissive mask.
+
+Terrain vertices grow from 24 to 28 bytes. The existing color/light fields and
+water/HDR metadata are unchanged; vertex attribute location 6 transports the
+new RGBA8 value in instanced and flat native material pipelines. Model normals
+are not added: Aurora reconstructs the visible geometric normal from fragment
+derivatives before divergent branches. Entities and the first-person hand do
+not use this terrain material API.
+
+Frame uniforms, scene snapshot, shadow bindings and cloud history match
+atmosphere.2. The world target still stores SDR/gamma colour. This extension
+does not provide full-scene HDR, exposure metering, indirect light transport,
+per-source block-light colours, or new reflection data. Aurora computes terrain
+illumination in linear light and compresses/encodes it before returning Surface;
+engine fog and water composition retain their existing display-space contract.
+
+Validation includes packed-layout and color-preservation tests, old/new material
+composition, the SDK checks on all option extrema, and the opt-in
+`local_pack_pipelines_on_gpu` harness. Set `HORIZON_VALIDATE_SHADER_PACK` to a
+pack and run the latter with `--ignored --nocapture` on a real GPU.
